  "all_ingredients_flat": "jowar (sorghum) batter, carrot, ground chia seeds, flaxseed powder, garlic powder, watermelon seeds, pumpkin seeds, sunflower seeds",
  "instructions": "Soak jowar (sorghum) overnight, then rinse and grind the next day to make batter. Mix all the ingredients. Transfer the mixture to a container (a loaf pan, for example) lined with parchment paper. Sprinkle some seeds (watermelon seeds, pumpkin seeds, sunflower seeds) on top. Bake for 30 to 40 minutes at 180 C in an air fryer. The upper side of the bread becomes crispy. Inside is moist. For more crispiness, slice the bread and and bake the slices for another 10 minutes at 180 C.",
